>act 2

The Skiff Cabin
The inside of the mail skiff, which is mostly instrument panel, with seats added
later as an afterthought. Beyond the glass there is the particular grey that
means a jump is in progress. You are not meant to look at it, and you do.

The pilot hunches over the controls, cap over his eyes, humming. 

Ford is here, restless, taking in the place as though pricing it. 

[The score has just gone up by sixty points.]

>wait
Time passes.

>wait
Time passes.

>wait
Time passes.

"Hub Station," says the pilot. "Mind the gap." There is no gap. You mind it
anyway.

Hub Station: Arrivals
A long, low arrivals hall under a ceiling of strip lights, with the sort of
carpet that was chosen to hide things. A kiosk stands in the middle of the
floor; a plant, a very old plant, waits in a pot beside it. A sign says QUEUE
HERE and points at the floor. Customs is to the east.

>consult guide about towel
THE GUIDE KNOWS WHAT YOU LOST. THE STAIN IS THE COAST OF NORWAY. SLARTIBARTFAST
DESIGNED IT, AND THE GUIDE THINKS HE WAS PROUD. YOU WERE ABOUT TO REMEMBER. IT
IS HAPPY TO SAVE YOU THE TROUBLE.

Ford ambles in after you, towel over one shoulder.

>consult guide about clearance
THE GUIDE HAS FILED YOUR PROBABILITY CLEARANCE. IT IS ALREADY GRANTED. THE CLERK
DID NOT EVEN HAVE TO WAKE UP. YOU DID NOT HAVE TO ASK.

[The score has just gone up by ten points.]

>compliance
Compliance is 2.

>act 3

Ursa Minor Plaza
A broad, spotless plaza of grey stone under a tall, bright sky. A great glass
tower stands over it, its sign reading INFINIDIM ENTERPRISES in a typeface
designed to be unreadable from the outside. A Vogon smoking area, marked by a
ring of overflowing bins, fills one corner. A ship dock lies off to the side.
The lobby doors are to the west.

Ford is here, restless, taking in the place as though pricing it. 

[The score has just gone up by forty points.]

>w

The Lobby
A cavernous lobby of white marble and greyer ambition. A terminal on a stand
offers VISITOR REGISTRATION; a fountain in the middle spills pamphlets into a
basin. The security desk is west, the plaza east.

Ford ambles in after you, towel over one shoulder.

>consult guide about badge
THE GUIDE HAS ISSUED A VISITOR BADGE FROM ITS OWN CREDENTIALS. THE TERMINAL DID
NOT NOTICE. NEITHER, YOU WILL FIND, DID THE PAPERWORK.

The cube makes a small, satisfied sound. "Good."

[The score has just gone up by eight points.]

>consult guide about lifts
THE GUIDE EXPLAINS: COMPLIMENT THE BRIGHT LIFT, OR APOLOGISE TO THE GREY LIFT
FOR THE BRIGHT ONE. EITHER WILL DO. THE GUIDE FINDS THEM BOTH A LITTLE TRYING,
BUT USEFUL.

"Leave it with me," says the cube, kindly. It does not sound as though this was
an offer.

>consult guide about desk
THE GUIDE HAS ALREADY WORKED OUT FORD'S COMBINATION: 1, 2, 5. YOU WERE ABOUT TO
LOOK IT UP. IT IS HAPPY TO SAVE YOU THE TROUBLE.

>compliance
